{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"vapid-ferrous-weaverbird","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\nA supported full-suite run can fail in `tests/unit/test_rp04_s4_llm_runtime_heldout.py::test_secret_absent_from_conflict_error_message` when the test replaces `anthropic.AsyncAnthropic` with a lambda before `pydantic_ai.providers.anthropic` is first imported. The dependency constructs an import-time union containing that attribute and raises `TypeError: unsupported operand type(s) for |: function and type`. Determine whether this is a production defect or order-dependent test isolation, and sweep sibling monkeypatch-before-lazy-import cases.\n\n## Investigation and repair plan\n- Reproduce the failure on current `origin/main` both in the polluted lazy-import order and in an isolated control order.\n- Trace the runtime import path and test seam, inspect history and adjacent tests, and prove one falsifiable root cause before repair.\n- Cite the intended test contract and classify production versus test-isolation ownership.\n- Inventory existing coverage and create or strengthen the smallest in-process oracle that forces the lazy-import state and asserts the secret-redaction contract still reaches its intended conflict error.\n- Apply the minimal remediation at the owned seam, then prove RED to GREEN, exact-defect mutation sensitivity, original-report replication, and sibling coverage.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Runtime evidence proves the import-order mechanism and distinguishes it from production secret-redaction behavior.\n- [ ] The in-process unit oracle forces a fresh Anthropic provider import after the monkeypatch and observes the contractual redacted conflict error rather than a dependency import `TypeError`.\n- [ ] The oracle is observed RED before repair, GREEN after repair, and RED again under an exact-defect mutation.\n- [ ] A bounded sweep identifies and disposes every sibling test that replaces an SDK runtime class before the corresponding pydantic-ai provider module is imported.\n- [ ] The original failing node and its supported relevant suite pass in both isolated and order-sensitive execution.\n- [ ] The ticket records the final RCA, caller/safety assessment, sibling disposition, and replication evidence.","id":"f89c-a724-981a-4416","parent_id":"","priority":1,"tags":["bug","test-isolation","llm-runtime"],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Anthropic class monkeypatch breaks lazy provider import"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787047945075228001,"uuid":"de5faee5-49b8-4795-a035-a192a9ae4050"}